WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.257
IaC automation usually needs credentials
to read current state and modify

2
00:00:07.337 --> 00:00:08.946
infrastructure.

3
00:00:09.026 --> 00:00:15.462
Those credentials may belong to a service
account, workload identity,

4
00:00:15.542 --> 00:00:20.690
cloud role, CI/CD runner, managed
deployment platform,

5
00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:23.667
or human-approved release job.

6
00:00:23.747 --> 00:00:25.999
Whatever form they take,

7
00:00:26.079 --> 00:00:33.587
they should be treated as sensitive
operational authority because they can change

8
00:00:33.667 --> 00:00:35.705
real infrastructure.

9
00:00:35.785 --> 00:00:40.183
Different jobs may need different
permissions.

10
00:00:40.263 --> 00:00:46.591
A formatting or module validation job may
not need cloud access at all.

11
00:00:46.671 --> 00:00:52.249
A plan job may need read access to state
and current resources.

12
00:00:52.329 --> 00:00:57.906
An apply job may need write access for a
specific environment.

13
00:00:57.986 --> 00:01:04.315
A rollback or break-glass workflow may
need a separate approval path.

14
00:01:04.395 --> 00:01:12.225
Treating every job as though it needs
broad administrator access creates unnecessary

15
00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:13.592
blast radius.

16
00:01:13.672 --> 00:01:19.786
Secrets should come from approved
secret-management mechanisms,

17
00:01:19.866 --> 00:01:25.229
platform identity, or workload identity
where practical.

18
00:01:25.309 --> 00:01:30.886
Avoid hard-coded credentials, broad
repository variables,

19
00:01:30.966 --> 00:01:36.866
copied local credentials, and shared cloud
administrator keys.

20
00:01:36.946 --> 00:01:44.132
Scope identities by environment, action,
service, repository, and workflow.

21
00:01:44.212 --> 00:01:51.720
A development plan should not accidentally
receive production apply privileges.

22
00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:56.520
Automation identities need lifecycle
management.

23
00:01:56.600 --> 00:02:03.679
Each credential should have an owner,
purpose, scope, environment boundary,

24
00:02:03.759 --> 00:02:09.015
rotation path, revocation process, and
review schedule.

25
00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:12.956
Least privilege is not a one-time setting.

26
00:02:13.036 --> 00:02:19.043
As repositories, modules, cloud services,
and pipelines evolve,

27
00:02:19.123 --> 00:02:26.095
the permissions behind IaC automation
should be reviewed and narrowed where

28
00:02:26.175 --> 00:02:27.140
possible.
